\procedure named()
A CLOSER CARRYING THE WRONG NAME CLOSES NOTHING. `\end` takes the definition's own name or none at
all, and a name failing to match leaves the definition open — the host reads a BLANK body and raises
`unterminated-definition`, exactly as a missing closer does, so the closer below reads as body text
nobody asked for.

This carrier stands alone, and carries its own explanation INSIDE the body, for two reasons a
definition imposes: an open definition consumes the rest of its source, so a second specimen behind
one never parses; and a pragma answers only at the top of a file, so a line of prose above one
retires it to body text.
\end other
